WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.440
- Watch this, 
I'm going to show you

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.800
something really fascinating.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.600
Do me a favor, Web Summit.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.720
I want you to stand 
up if the following

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.880
statement is true.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.400
I know some of you 
are fucking lazy,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.320
but it's good circulation, 
so if this

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.840
is true to you, stand up.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.640
How many people here
now, actually get upset

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.590
when another 
human being calls them?

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.470
Stand up.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.291
Gonna wait.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.600
I want everybody, 
don't sit down yet.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.960
I want everybody 
to look at this.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.640
These are human beings,
I'm going to repeat it

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.600
to everybody, these are
human beings that actually

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.880
get upset when 
another person calls them.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.640
The main way we rolled,
just five or six years ago.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.480
Let's clap it up 
for these pioneers.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.000
(audience applause)

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.320
I'll tell you why I'm clapping
for that pioneer right there.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.840
I'm clapping, because what
these people have innately felt,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.519
and understood, is the
emergence of the most important

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.920
asset in our new ecosystem,
along with the

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.080
health of our family, 
money, our religion,

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.960
and the health, which is, time.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.600
The reason those people
stood up, and were mad,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.560
that somebody called 
them is because we

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.120
have technology now, that
allows us to actually text

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.120
somebody, and I'll call
you back on my time,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.520
don't call me on your time.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.000
Like, literally, like...

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.120
"Fuckin', I'll text 
you back, mom!"

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:34.960
That kind of shit.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.880
(audience laughter)

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.255
And so, we as business
people, in Corporate America,

00:01:41.255 --> 00:01:45.163
need to wrap our head
around one very big truth.

00:01:45.163 --> 00:01:47.739
The day of advertising,

00:01:47.739 --> 00:01:50.100
stealing somebody's time,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.589
is over.

00:01:51.589 --> 00:01:54.141
(upbeat music)

